course: dictionary
lesson: 1459
title: Context and a kind gift
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing and show what it is used for. The sentences around a word give you clues. «Mrs Platt is first at the door with a casserole and a shovel for the drive.» People do not carry a shovel to a door for a drink, so a casserole must be something you can carry to someone, probably food.
explain: Look at the words around the new word. A casserole is cooked slowly in the oven, with meat, vegetables or beans, in some liquid. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "a dish of food with a shovel for the drive" still makes sense, so your idea is right.
explain: Context also shows what people do and feel. «It comes and goes like waves, and people show it in many ways, from tears to casseroles on the doorstep.» Tears and casseroles are both ways of showing care, so a casserole can be a kind gift, not just a dinner.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Casserole» means a dish of meat, vegetables or beans cooked slowly in the oven in liquid.
fact: A casserole dish is the deep pot with a lid that the food is cooked in.
fact: In some areas of America, a casserole is called a «hotdish».
fact: Bringing a casserole to a neighbour who is ill or grieving is a kind way to help.
exercise: «Mrs Platt is first at the door with a casserole.» What is a casserole? | *A dish of meat, vegetables or beans cooked slowly in the oven | A kind of bicycle | A wind chime | A pair of shoes
exercise: What is a casserole dish? | A dish that is served cold | *The deep pot with a lid that the food is cooked in | A wide, flat plate for cakes | A small cup for tea
exercise: «Mrs Platt is first at the door with a casserole and a shovel for the drive.» Find and copy the word for something she brings to help clear the ice. | *shovel | bikes | casserole | door
test: «The casserole was cooked slowly in the oven.» What does this tell you about a casserole? | It was made of paper and glue | It was a kind of bicycle | *It was cooked slowly in the oven in some liquid | It was eaten cold straight from a shop
test: In some parts of America, a casserole is called what? | Sandwich | Soup in a cup | *Hotdish | Pudding
exam: Jayden reads, «She took a casserole round to her ill neighbour.» What does casserole mean here? | *A dish of meat, vegetables or beans cooked slowly in the oven | A kind of wind chime | A shovel for the drive | A bicycle for the ice
